# One person, four spellings.
#
# `git log` showed SysAdminDoc, Matthew Parker, Matt Parker and Matthew as four
# separate contributors, and GitHub listed the last of them separately because
# it was authored from a second account. This maps them onto one identity for
# every git tool that honours .mailmap: shortlog, blame, log --author.
#
# GitHub's own contributor list is computed from raw commit metadata and does
# NOT read this file. Collapsing it there needs a history rewrite with
# git-filter-repo and a force push, which stays a separate deliberate decision.

SysAdminDoc <matt_parker@outlook.com> <matt_parker@outlook.com>
SysAdminDoc <matt_parker@outlook.com> Matthew Parker <matt_parker@outlook.com>
SysAdminDoc <matt_parker@outlook.com> Matt Parker <matt_parker@outlook.com>
SysAdminDoc <matt_parker@outlook.com> Matthew <snafumatthew@gmail.com>
